course: dictionary
lesson: 5837
title: Make: one word, many jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Make is a small word with many meanings, so do not guess from the word alone. Read the words around it to find the job it is doing. «Salt from sea spray or from gritted winter roads makes iron rust faster, so cars and railings by the sea rust quickly.» Here makes means causes: the salt causes the iron to change and rust faster.
explain: Sometimes make means creates or builds something. «Swapping quickly between costumes, slightly different pictures of a sprite, makes animation, like a flip book.» Ask yourself: what is being made? Here the answer is animation, so makes means creates.
explain: Use the swap check. Put a simple word like causes, creates or builds in place of make. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning. «If Gran says "keep the change", telling her how much is left makes it an honest gift.» Makes it an honest gift means causes it to be honest.
fact: Make means to build, cook or create something, as in make a cake.
fact: Make can mean to cause something to happen or be, as in «The joke made me laugh.»
fact: In maths, make can mean to come to a total: 3 and 4 make 7. «Make 10» means find numbers that add up to 10.
fact: Make also appears in everyday phrases: make a mistake, make friends, make sure, and make do (manage with what you have).
fact: Make is a verb with four forms: make, makes, made and making. Made is the past tense, as in «I made a card yesterday.»
exercise: «Salt from sea spray makes iron rust faster.» What does makes mean here? | Adds up to a total | Says sorry | Builds something new | *Causes a change
exercise: In maths, «3 and 4 make 7.» What does make mean? | Cook a meal | Create a picture | *Come to a total | Force someone to act
exercise: In «Swapping quickly between costumes, slightly different pictures of a sprite, makes animation», find and copy the thing that is made. | *animation | costumes | flip book | sprite
test: «The joke made me laugh.» What does made mean here? | Cooked | Earned | Built | *Caused me to
test: Which phrase means manage with what you have? | make a mistake | make sure | *make do | make friends
exam: In «telling her how much is left makes it an honest gift», what does makes mean? | Adds it up to a total | Forces it on her | *Causes it to be | Builds it from scratch
